course: dictionary
lesson: 5720
title: A coin called a loonie
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. «In Canada the one-dollar coin is called a loonie, because it has a loon on it, and the two-dollar coin is called a toonie.» A loon is a water bird, so the clue tells you the loonie is a coin with a bird on it.
explain: «3 toonies and 2 loonies make 3 × 2 + 2 = 8 dollars.» Money words sit next to numbers and prices, so here loonie means a coin worth one dollar. Try it: swap in "one-dollar coin" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Loonie is informal, which means it is a friendly everyday word, not a word for official writing. In the UK and Australia, looney or loony can mean a crazy or silly person, and that use can be rude. Look at the words around it to tell which meaning is which.
fact: A loonie is a Canadian one-dollar coin with a loon, a water bird, on it.
fact: A toonie is a Canadian two-dollar coin.
fact: 3 toonies and 2 loonies make 3 × 2 + 2 = 8 dollars.
fact: Loonie can also mean the Canadian dollar as money, as in «the loonie went up».
fact: Loonie is informal, and the spelling looney or loony can mean a crazy or silly person, which can be rude.
exercise: «In Canada the one-dollar coin is called a loonie.» What is a loonie? | A water bird | *A one-dollar coin from Canada | A two-dollar coin from Canada | A crazy person
exercise: «3 toonies and 2 loonies make 3 × 2 + 2 = 8 dollars.» How many dollars is one toonie worth? | 8 dollars | 1 dollar | *2 dollars | 3 dollars
exercise: Why is the coin called a loonie? | Because it is worth ten dollars | *Because it shows a loon, a water bird | Because it is shiny and round
test: «To count the money, each toonie gives 2 dollars and each loonie gives 1 dollar; add the two amounts.» If you have 4 loonies, how many dollars is that? | *4 dollars | 6 dollars | 8 dollars | 2 dollars
test: Mia reads, «The loonie went up this week.» What does loonie mean here? | *The Canadian dollar as money | A crazy or silly person | A water bird | A two-dollar coin
exam: Loonie is an informal word; which meaning is rude, and where is it used? | *A crazy or silly person, used in the UK and Australia | A water bird | A one-dollar coin in Canada | The Canadian dollar as money
